## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of module composition, workspace-based state, and simple CI gates in a beginner-friendly way. It ensures the candidate can wire a wrapper for consistent tagging across environments and validate constraints early in CI.

## Key Concepts

- Terraform modules and wrappers
- Variable validation for environment constraints
- Workspaces and workspace-aware backends
- Per-env state isolation with a single backend
- GitHub Actions gates around terraform plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// modules/env-wrapper/variables.tf
variable "environment" {
  type = string
  description = "Environment name (dev, prod)"
  validation {
    condition = contains(["dev","prod"], var.environment)
    error_message = "environment must be 'dev' or 'prod'"
  }
}
variable "cost_center" {
  type = string
}
```

```javascript
// modules/env-wrapper/main.tf
locals {
  common_tags = {
    Environment = var.environment
    CostCenter  = var.cost_center
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience with governance, cross-repo data sharing, and policy-as-code in real fintech environments.

## Key Concepts
- cost-governance patterns
- terraform_remote_state data source
- policy as code (OPA)
- CI gating of plans

## Code Example
```javascript
# Minimal budget fetch (pseudo-terraform)
data "terraform_remote_state" "budget" {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "gov-budgets";
    key    = "costs/${var.env}.tfstate";
    region = "us-east-1";
  }
}
locals {
  monthly_budget = data.terraform_remote_state.budget.outputs["monthly_budget"]
}
```
```javascript
# Minimal OPA policy sketch
package terraform.costs
deny[msg] {
  planned_cost := input.planned_cost
  budget := input.monthly_budget
  planned_cost > budget
  msg = sprintf("Budget exceeded: %v > %v", planned_cost, budget)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this to handle multi-region budgets?
- How would you add tests to verify gating behavior in CI?
